<title>HONG KONG: HK Sept retail sales up 7.0 pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Sept retail sales up 7.0 pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong September retail sales totalled a provisional HK$18.5 billion, up seven percent on the year and down three percent on the month, Census and Statistics Department figures showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets:</p>
<p>						     Sept     Aug</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on year)  - value   +7	 +5</p>
<p>					 - volume  +3	 +1.5</p>
<p>			  (on month) - value   -3	 +1</p>
<p>					 - volume  -4	 +1</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on year)</p>
<p>  Clothing and footwear	  - value   +4	 +9</p>
<p>					 - volume  -4	 +1</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p>  clocks, valuable gifts	 - value   +5	 +4</p>
<p>					 - volume  +3	 +2</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p>  excluding cars		   - value   +7	 +9</p>
<p>					 - volume  +6	 +8</p>
<p>  Department stores		- value   +9	 +5</p>
<p>					 - volume  +4	 +1</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value   +2	 +5</p>
<p>					 - volume  -3	 -1</p>
<p> Fuels				 - value   -8	 -13</p>
<p>					 - volume  -13	-18</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value   +22	+8</p>
<p>					 - volume  +21	+7</p>
<p>Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value   +8	 -8</p>
<p>					 - volume  +8	 -6</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
